<title>USA: National Steel sees two pct rise in job costs.</title>
<headline>National Steel sees two pct rise in job costs.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Steel Corp said a wage increase for workers will raise its employment costs by about two percent and comes as no surprise.</p>
<p>&quot;It's actually lower than we had built into our strategic plan. It's not a shock,&quot; said spokesman Leon Judd.</p>
<p>The Mishawaka, Ind.-based steelmaker said Friday that 7,000 of its employees represented by the United Steelworkers won wage increases through an arbitration decision.</p>
<p>The wage hikes came on reopener negotiations on a contract good through 1999.  No further reopener is expected and the contract remains good through 1999, Judd said.</p>
